+      7. Final Approval. No newly constructed or altered public swimming pool shall be placed into
+operation until a final inspection of the facility has been conducted and a written approval to be placed into
+operation is issued by the Department. Before the final inspection can be conducted three (3) letters must
+be submitted, one by the pool contractor; one by the general contractor, owner or his designated agent; and
+one by the project architect or engineer; certifying that the public swimming pool, bathhouse, minimum
+toilet facilities, if required, fence, equipment room, area lighting, if provided, and other applicable items
+have been constructed according to approved plans and specifications and is ready for the final inspection.
+All three letters must be received by the Department before a final inspection will be conducted. In addition
+to the three certification letters, the engineer and or the architect or their representative must complete a
+copy of the Department’s final inspection checklist, and it must be submitted to the Department prior to the
+final inspection. A contractor’s and owner’s representative must be present at the time of the final
+inspection.
