<div class="post-inner thin "><div class="entry-content"><h3 id="mg-heading-6" class="wp-block-heading">ASHI Proposed Standard of Practice Changes</h3><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thank you to all&nbsp;who participated in the recent vote regarding the proposed&nbsp;<a href="https://www.homeinspector.org/proposed-ashi-standards-of-practice-public-changes/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Standard of Practice (SOP)</a>, which&nbsp;closed on January 8, 2026. Learn all about it <a href="https://www.homeinspector.org/proposed-ashi-standards-of-practice-public-changes/" type="link" id="https://www.homeinspector.org/proposed-ashi-standards-of-practice-public-changes/">here</a>.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>We are pleased to share that the SOP was approved, with a majority of the membership voting in favor.&nbsp;</strong>Your engagement and thoughtful participation in this process are appreciated and reflect the strength of our organization.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">As we move forward, additional information will be provided regarding the implementation date. The leadership team will work through the details of this process and communicate next steps, timelines, and guidance&nbsp;as they become available. Until the implementation date, the Standard of Practice below is the current version.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph">ASHI’s Standard of Practice is your blueprint for high-quality inspections. Deliver consistent, trusted results that set you apart from the competition.</p><div class="wp-block-columns alignwide is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-b5f34c20 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex"><div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow" style="flex-basis:66.66%"><div class="mg-block mg-accordion mb-16 border-0 block-mg-accordion mt-8" data-allow-toggle data-allow-multiple><h3 class="border-b-0 py-0 my-0  format-list" data-ctr="1"> <button id="accordion-item-block_4196045e979f508a2fc74f35cab0056e-0" cla