+  <div class="paragraph paragraph--type--accordion-options paragraph--view-mode--default accordion-item">
+                  <h2 class="accordion-header accordion-header-hover my-0" id="heading-5926">
+          <button class="accordion-button py-4 collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse-5926" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse-5926">
+            <span class="text-holder">
+            Summary of Regulation 72-1: Dams and Reservoirs Safety Act Regulations
+            </span>
+            <span class="icon-holder">
+                <svg height="12" width="12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
+                <line y1="0" y2="12" x1="6" x2="6"  stroke-width="3" class="accordion_icon vertical-line collapsed" />
+                <line  x1="0" x2="12" y1="6" y2="6"  stroke-width="3" class="accordion_icon"  />
+              </svg>
+            </span>
+          </button>
+        </h2>
+        <div id="collapse-5926" class="accordion-collapse collapse " aria-labelledby="heading-5926">
+          <div class="accordion-body">
+            
+            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-html-text field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>The regulations were initially approved in 1977 and they were most recently amended in July of 1997. The regulations for the most part mirror the requirements of the SC Dams and Reservoirs Safety Act. The regulations create a tiered permitting program based on a classification system of dams. Dams regulated by the Department are classified based on size and hazards. The size classifications are large, intermediate, small, and very small. Hazard classifications are high hazard, significant hazard, and low hazard.</p><p>These regulations specify the administrative process for obtaining a permit for either a new dam or the alteration, repair, or removal of an existing dam. The items required to be submitted to the Department as part of the permit application package are also given in the regulations as well as some general design criteria a dam must meet.</p></div>
